From 608b2e97aad139044e5c1d8dda0af8b7443a1079 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ajrat Makhmutov <rauty@altlinux.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:31:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plymouth): Wait for the Wayland greeter to connect

Wayland display readiness can precede compositor startup. Quitting
Plymouth at that point can expose the text console. A greeter that
never connects can leave processes blocked in plymouth --wait, so the
handoff needs a bounded wait.
